GATE="secrets"
EXPECT_EXIT="1"
EXPECT_RULE="generic-api-key"
DESCRIPTION="Also asserts a denominator. EXPECT_SCANNED_MIN existed with no fault using it, so direction 2 asserted nothing about scope at all -- the mechanism added to catch a gate examining less than it claims was itself unexercised. A committed cloud credential must be caught. Expected rule is generic-api-key, observed rather than assumed: gitleaks 8.30.1 does not fire an AWS-specific rule on a bare AKIA identifier, and this fault originally asserted a rule id that does not exist in that config. The exit code was right and the reason was wrong, which is the entire argument for asserting the rule and not only the exit code."
EXPECT_SCANNED_MIN="2"
